The boy band shared the 14-track sequence in a black, white and red graphic on Instagram and Weverse, revealing that the set will begin with a track called &#8220;Body to Body&#8221; followed by the songs &#8220;Hooligan,&#8221; &#8220;Aliens,&#8221; &#8220;FYA,&#8221; &#8220;2.0,&#8221; &#8220;No. 29&#8221; and &#8220;SWIM.&#8221;

If the amount of songs on the listing wasn&#8217;t dizzying enough, the septet comprised of RM, Jin, Suga, j-hope, Jimin, V and Jung Kook will also release a song called &#8220;Merry Go Round,&#8221; which precedes the tracks &#8220;NORMAL,&#8221; &#8220;Like Animals,&#8221; &#8220;they don&#8217;t know &#8217;bout us,&#8221; &#8220;One More Night&#8221; and &#8220;Please.&#8221;

Also revealed Tuesday were the producers and songwriters on the album, showing that members of the band had hands in penning all of the tracks. A-list hitmakers such as Diplo, Tame Impala&#8217;s Kevin Parker, Mike WiLL Made-It and Ryan Tedder are credited as producers on different songs.

Arirang is set to arrive on March 20, marking the group&#8217;s first full-band album in six years. The Bangtan Boys&#8217; last full set, Be, debuted at No. 1 on the Billboard 200 in 2020 and produced Billboard Hot 100 -topping hits &#8220;Life Goes On&#8221; and &#8220;Dynamite.&#8221;

ARMY hasn&#8217;t yet heard any of the songs on ARIRANG ahead of its release, but the band may have hidden a clue as to which title will serve as the lead single in the tracklist graphic. While all of the other 13 songs are highlighted in red, Track 7 &#8212; &#8220;SWIM&#8221; &#8212; is highlighted in black. Plus, the hashtag &#8220;BTS_SWIM&#8221; is included in the post&#8217;s caption on Instagram.

